        "id": "error-detection",
        "name": "Error Detection & Grammar"
      },
      "category": "English",
      "question": "[Sample] Identify the segment in the sentence which contains a grammatical error: \"Neither the manager nor his assistants was present at the annual review meeting.\"",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "Neither the manager"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "nor his assistants"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "was present"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "at the annual review meeting"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "explanation": "With \"Neither ... nor\", the verb agrees with the closer subject (\"assistants\", plural). Replace \"was present\" with \"were present\".",
      "exam": {
        "name": "SSC CGL",
        "year": 2024,
        "shift": "Shift 2"
      },
      "difficulty": "Easy",
      "source": {
